## A. FRANCIS STATUS SUMMARY

FRANCIS status: Stage 17 documentation packet is complete as a provisional technical-manual section. Physical validation is not complete.

- Current state: FR-017 forearm cuffs are defined as left/right-specific, padded, adjustable, removable, inspectable pilot-interface components.
- Recovered source material: no prior FR-017 forearm-cuff document, image, checklist, or draft was found in the accessible local workspace. This packet uses the active prompt as the governing fallback specification.
- Documentation completion percentage: 25/25 required Stage 17 packet deliverables documented, 100 percent documentation coverage.
- Evidence-container completion percentage: 22/22 support records created in `FR-017_Stage17_Package`, including measurement intake template, safety-critical landmark confirmation fields, mockup build template, mannequin interface input template, pilot static fit input template, pilot movement input template, quick-release/cable-snag input template, engineering review input template, validation gate chain runbook, final audit, and manifest; physical evidence remains pending.
- Physical validation completion percentage: 0 percent. No measurements, mannequin tests, pilot static tests, pilot movement tests, load tests, or professional engineering review records were available.
- Highest-risk unresolved issue: neurovascular compression or movement restriction caused by cuff strap placement, padding shape, cable routing, or hidden releases.
- Next concrete action: mark and confirm safety-critical landmarks, collect left/right forearm measurements, complete the non-powered mockup build record, complete the mannequin interface test record, complete pilot static and movement fit records, complete quick-release/cable-snag evidence, then obtain professional engineering review before any final physical completion audit, powered test, or frame-coupled test.

Stage 17 is not complete for physical use until all failed or unvalidated fit, release, circulation, nerve, wrist, elbow, glove-removal, and cable-snag conditions are closed by evidence.

