### 7. Material Options

Permitted provisional material families:

- Skin-side layer: breathable spacer mesh, athletic lining textile, moisture-resistant soft sleeve, or removable washable liner.
- Padding: EVA foam, Poron-style impact/compression foam, neoprene foam, or layered removable foam shims.
- Semi-rigid support: thermoformed polyethylene, flexible TPU, thin composite-safe plastic, or 3D printed nylon/TPU blend for non-load-bearing shells.
- Straps: broad nylon webbing, elastic-limited webbing, hook-and-loop wrap bands, or low-profile textile ladder adjustment.
- Release tabs: textile pull loops, low-profile polymer buckle tabs, or guarded pull-cord release.

Material exclusions for first prototype:

- Sharp carbon edges against pilot-facing zones.
- Hard metal buckles on inner forearm.
- Narrow cord tension bands.
- Adhesive-only retention where release is safety-critical.
- Any material that claims ballistic, powered, or structural performance without test evidence.

### 8. COTS Component Options

Allowed COTS candidates for non-powered mockup:

- Broad webbing straps, 38 mm to 50 mm class, subject to fit testing.
- Low-profile side-release buckles placed on outer forearm only.
- Hook-and-loop panels with rounded ends and anti-scratch edge binding.
- Removable foam pad inserts.
- Sewn pull tabs with tactile identification.
- Flexible cable sleeve or textile wire channel.
- Low-profile snaps or non-load-bearing alignment markers.

COTS caution: no purchased component is considered certified for FRANCIS use until its documentation, fit behavior, failure mode, and release behavior are reviewed.

### 9. Custom Fabrication Options

Custom fabrication may include:

- Patterned left/right textile cuff sleeves.
- Sewn outer cable sleeve with removable retention loops.
- Thermoformed outer forearm locator panel.
- 3D printed non-load-bearing alignment tabs with rounded edges.
- Replaceable padding kit with labeled thicknesses.
- Quick-release pull-tab housing that remains exposed after frame/armor mockup installation.
- Pressure-mapping test inserts for development only.

Fabrication rule: every custom part must preserve inspection, cleaning, removal, and emergency release.

### 10. Future R&D Options

Future options are not current validated capability:

- Distributed soft pressure sensing for fit monitoring.
- Latch state sensing tied to FR-149.
- Cable-disconnect detection for FR-163.
- Glove/wrist assembly removal interlock readback.
- Mannequin-mounted motion capture for elbow/wrist clearance.
- Instrumented strap tension logging.
- Comparative left/right asymmetry fit library.

